roblem asks whether two smooth manifolds without boundary that have the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msame universal cover and fundamental group are necessarily diffeomorphic.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mGiven: M and N are smooth manifolds without boundary. They have the same [0m
[38;2;124;124;124muniversal cover (say $\tilde{M}$) and the same fundamental group $\pi_1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe question: are M and N necessarily diffeomorphic?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about the structure. If M has universal cover $\tilde{M}$ and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfundamental group $\pi_1$, then M = $\tilde{M} / \pi_1$ where $\pi_1$ acts on $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\tilde{M}$ by deck transformations. Similarly N = $\tilde{M} / \pi_1$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBut the key point is: the action of $\pi_1$ on $\tilde{M}$ could be different! [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mTwo different actions of the same group on the same space can produce different [0m[38;2;124;124;124mquotients.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the question becomes: can the same group act on the same universal cover in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtwo different ways (as deck transformations, i.e., freely and properly [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdiscontinuously) producing non-diffeomorphic quotients?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think of examples.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mClassic example: Lens spaces. Consider $S^3$ as the universal cover. The [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfundamental group is $\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}$. Different actions of $\mathbb{Z}/[0m[38;2;124;124;124mp\mathbb{Z}$ on $S^3$ give different lens spaces $L(p,q)$. [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSpecifically, $S^3 = \{(z_1, z_2) \in \mathbb{C}^2 : |z_1|^2 + |z_2|^2 = 1\}$. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mThe action of $\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}$ generated by $(z_1, z_2) \mapsto (e^{2\pi[0m[38;2;124;124;124mi/p} z_1, e^{2\pi i q/p} z_2)$ gives the lens space $L(p,q)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBoth $L(p, q_1)$ and $L(p, q_2)$ have universal cover $S^3$ and fundamental [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgroup $\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, are $L(p, q_1)$ and $L(p, q_2)$ always diffeomorphic? No! For example, [0m
